{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793877975,"nonce":"QwkBcAEvSgy2frZcoOzUV3gZMx8=","title":"Python OSR assertion can outlive its fixed-work loop's execution window","message":"During validation of collector-managed drops (399bcda), a_frame_in_the_outlined_region_moves_to_the_optimizing_tier failed once in the full --test-threads=2 suite while other local validation work was active. The process returned the correct checksum 25574991424 and exited successfully. It transferred from the interpreter to the Cranelift outlined region and requested LLVM; stderr ended after LLVM installation started and the OSR live-in layout was printed, before helper publication/transfer. There was no verifier error.\n\nThe fixture long_single_call.py runs a fixed 50,000,000-iteration loop, then exits. Its test requires an LLVM transfer before exit, so compilation scheduling can determine the assertion independently of program correctness. The observed failure is not being added to any known-failure allowlist and no baseline/assertion has been weakened.\n\nEight isolated repetitions each of the previous committed binary, the new binary with early release, and the new binary with collector-managed drops all returned the correct checksum and demonstrated the required LLVM transfer (24/24). This supports a timing-dependent test finding, but does not by itself prove which contention caused the original failure.\n\nEvidence: /private/tmp/zyntax-gc-drop-fixed/tests.log (original failure), osr-check.json and osr-check.log (all three arms), and osr-suite-isolated.log (complete isolated rerun). Investigate deterministic publication/transfer coordination for this test without requiring a short production process to wait for unused background compilation.","files":null}]}